 "description": "C.2's stage 2 on benchmark v4, held to the network's graded regime (description, discarded seeds).\n\nEvery stage-2 design so far ended with outputs the senses barely move: stage 1 with a silent\nnetwork, the unbounded runs with a saturated readout, the soft-capped runs with 97% of motor neurons\nsaturated (`network_gain.json`). Here, applied in this script (no package code changes):\n\n- the box: the three wiring scales on [0, 0.75] (the encoder's own graded range) and every sensory\n  gain on [-2, 2], each mapped onto the encoder's unit box; every other range unchanged;\n- the readout: each output's pre-squash value through 2\u00b7tanh(x / 2), and four fitted pool centres\n  on [-1, 1], so the readout is b + \u03a3_j w_j (pool_j - c_j);\n- the guard: each simulation tallies its motor neurons' saturation (the share of steps with\n  |h| > 0.99, over every animal), and a candidate with over half its motor neurons saturated in\n  over half the steps scores 500 more, behind every responsive candidate and ahead of any with an\n  undefined statistic.\n\nFrom the staged pilot's stage-1 answer (inside the new box, so its worm is unchanged), centres at 0,\nsigma0 0.1, on the corrected wiring, scored by v4's ranking score on D_fit; CMA 9473; fit animals\n706,000,000 + 200\u00b7k + i; cap 200 on 16 workers. Every 50 generations the answer is profiled (each\noutput's bounded pre-squash percentiles, the primitive shares, the time on the lawn, the motor\nsaturation and each food feature's gain onto the pools; one 1,800-s reference episode, seed\n99,670,000) and graded on D_fit's assays on one population (707,000,000 + 200\u00b7c + i). Run from the\nrepository root.\n",
